	4. Technical Specifications & Mathematical Formulations
The implementation of ClayGameOfLifeEngine relies on the following core mathematical foundations:


* Conway's B3/S23 State Transition Rule on Discrete 2-Torus:
$$\text{State}{t+1}(x, y) = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if } \text{State}t(x, y) = 1 \text{ and } N(x, y) \in {2, 3} \ 1 & \text{if } \text{State}t(x, y) = 0 \text{ and } N(x, y) = 3 \ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}$$
Where $N(x, y)$ represents the sum of Moore neighborhood states wrapped toroidally:
$$x{\text{left}} = (x - 1 + W) \pmod W, \quad x{\text{right}} = (x + 1) \pmod W$$
$$y{\text{up}} = (y - 1 + H) \pmod H, \quad y_{\text{down}} = (y + 1) \pmod H$$
